    "result_text": "The test passes. The change is implemented full-stack:\n\n- **Database** \u2014 `V11__client_counts_indexes.sql` adds additive indexes on `projects(client_id)` and `contacts(client_id)` to support the per-client count lookups.\n- **Server** \u2014 new endpoint `GET /api/clients/{id}/summary` (new YAML + `GetClientSummary` logic class + `ClientSummaryView`) returning `{ projectCount, contactCount }` via `COUNT(*)` keyed by `client_id`.\n- **Front-end** \u2014 the clients feature now renders a `ClientSummaryBadges` component when a client is opened, fetching that endpoint and exposing `client-projects-count` (`2`) and `client-contacts-count` (`3`) exactly as the spec asserts.\n\nEverything is additive and local \u2014 a new endpoint file, new classes, a new migration, and a new component composed into the existing client detail view without touching shared routing or other features. The existing `/__test__` seed already covered clients, projects, and contacts, so no seed changes were needed.",
